cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software when using the VRET CLI/CUDA line."
type: software
title: "VRET: Verified Reduction & Execution Toolkit (CLI + CUDA checkpoint)"
authors:
  - name: "VRET contributors"
version: 0.2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Gaijin-01/VRET"
url: "https://github.com/Gaijin-01/VRET"
date-released: 2026-11-02
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  VRET CLI and its immutable CUDA/GPU checkpoint, version 0.2.0. A
  standard-library command line front end that re-verifies a hash-pinned
  checkpoint against its bundled receipts and drives the strict, bulk and
  pipelined CUDA execution paths. Published with the checkpoint included, so
  the reported screening throughput and physical-equivalence results can be
  reproduced from the installed artifact. The correctness oracle is the CPU
  evaluator; GPU results are compared against it bitwise. Not a production
  service and not a stable SDK, and not a claim about any cryptographic
  circuit: the checkpoint's cryptography is SHA-256 prefix matching only.
